can include the 2e version of Belial's Brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>definitely look forward to the athanor supplement and knights templar overview","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T16:24:46-08:00","id":1278451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1259978-cofd-to-be-added-to-the-storyteller-s-vault?p=1278219#post1278219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here are some of the things I've got cooking (most of which are Dark Eras related):<br /> <br /> - An athanor supplement for Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Athanors, you say? Any chance of including ones that alter the effects of existing Distillations (like Fetishes can do to Gifts), so as to have a way to add &quot;new&quot; powers to Promethean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T16:33:18-08:00","id":1278726,"title":"","content":"Got my 2nd edition of Blood Sorcery finished!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/263371.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\"> Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation - Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation takes the systems presented in Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies, and updates </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-05T15:01:56-08:00","id":1278872,"title":"","content":"Well, my first submitted content to the Storyteller's Vault has just gone up! Oddly enough, it's for Requiem 2e, not Forsaken 2e - I have Forsaken material in the pipeline but I still feel a bit like I'm somehow letting the werewolf side down a bit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, you can find the product, Spectral Hunger, at:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263438/Spectral-Hunger\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/263438.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263438/Spectral-Hunger\" target=\"_blank\"> Spectral Hunger - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263438/Spectral-Hunger\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263438/Spectral-Hunger </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Spectral Hunger - The world shivers in invisible frequencies, unseen maggots writhing just beneath its skin. Ghosts, spirits, and worse be </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Spectral Hunger is a short sourcebook detailing a new Discipline and two new Ordo Dracul Mysteries that deal with the ephemeral beings who plague the Chronicles of Darkness: ghosts, spirits, and the Strix themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T09:37:32-08:00","id":1278979,"title":"","content":"I'm debating writing up a couple supplements, but I'm not sure where to start, so I'd like a little input from the community. If people could let me know what they'd like to see, or springboard off of these concepts with their own ideas, that would be fantastic. I'll list my concepts below:<ul><li><b>Blue Book: </b>Something about mortals with Supernatural Merits and/or access to Rites or Ceremonies; potentially building things like Medium into a Merit-based micro template. Expect a lot about folklore, magical practices in different cultures around the world (including Dark Eras content), Mystery Cults (including my Merit-based Organization rules), and how mortals with Supernatural Merits can &quot;punch up&quot; in games with a mixed cast. I'm debating sprucing up my Pacts rules, playing with the Fate optional rule, and using the Favours mechanic from <b>Requiem for Regina</b> to make Social Merits a little more fluid and dynamic. Possibly adding some inter-Merit synergy as well.</li> <li><b>Vampire: </b>A conversion of Threnodies from <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</b> to Second Edition. Possibly add some other tweaks to how things like Blood Sorcery, Oaths, and Laws work. Bringing the Strix more in line with the standard Ephemeral Being rules. Possibly some Dark Eras content <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>'s <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire\" target=\"_blank\">BITE ME: How to Write Vampire</a> has me inspired and I'm percolating on how to play with the concept of the First Tradition, different attitudes towards and methods of feeding, how vampires relate to others, and different ways to Climb the Ladder or Spin the Web. Also, stuff for the Half-Damned, and possibly something about designing Clans.</li> <li><b>Werewolf:</b> Something akin to a Night Horrors book. Lots of Spirits, lots of territories; things about how I see the Hisil's ecology. Possibly stuff set in the Sundered World, or dealing with remnants of the Border Marches, that's seriously caught my imagination. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>'s particular brand of body horror, animism, and Spirit-empowered witchcraft is a current I can definitely swim in, so I'm also pondering writing a ton of Rites and playing with Influences a bit. Possibly making something for Rank 6+ Spirits (and Ephemeral Beings in general) inspired by <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, the rules for Things That Should Not Be from <b>Second Sight</b>, and some of the unofficial Rank 6+ Pangaeans.</li> <li><b>Mage: </b>There is an absolutely absurd amount of Dark Eras stuff frothing in my brain here, especially when it comes to concepts like Great Cults, Darshanas, and how the Mutapa Mages were presented in <b>Princes of the Conquered Land</b>. More cross-splat weirdness inspired by the aforesaid Dark Era, overhauls of Artifacts, Imbued Items, and Supernal Summoning (possibly Supernal Beings in general). Reworking Mage Sight to slot into the Investigation rules, and the Duel Arcane more properly into either Social Maneuvering or Chases. A whole lot of stuff on how I see the Supernal World (and why it isn't really separate or distant from the Fallen World), how to portray Mages in ways that fit folklore and traditional practices more closely than pop culture, emphasizing the drift Mages experience from human to something Other, and how to work with Mages so they don't completely overwhelm other magic users in the setting.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 01-06-2019, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T10:49:53-08:00","id":1278995,"title":"","content":"Does anyone know of any good page layout/design software that's compatible with a Chromebook? I have at least one thing I'd like to take a shot at publishing, but don't own a Windows or Mac computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T11:22:29-08:00","id":1279001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1259978-cofd-to-be-added-to-the-storyteller-s-vault?p=1278979#post1278979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm debating writing up a couple supplements, but I'm not sure where to start, so I'd like a little input from the community. If people could let me know what they'd like to see, or springboard off of these concepts with their own ideas, that would be fantastic. I'll list my concepts below:<ul><li><b>Blue Book: </b>Something about mortals with Supernatural Merits and/or access to Rites or Ceremonies; potentially building things like Medium into a Merit-based micro template. Expect a lot about folklore, magical practices in different cultures around the world (including Dark Eras content), Mystery Cults (including my Merit-based Organization rules), and how mortals with Supernatural Merits can &quot;punch up&quot; in games with a mixed cast. I'm debating sprucing up my Pacts rules, playing with the Fate optional rule, and using the Favours mechanic from <b>Requiem for Regina</b> to make Social Merits a little more fluid and dynamic. Possibly adding some inter-Merit synergy as well.</li> <li><b>Vampire: </b>A conversion of Threnodies from <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies</b> to Second Edition. Possibly add some other tweaks to how things like Blood Sorcery, Oaths, and Laws work. Bringing the Strix more in line with the standard Ephemeral Being rules. Possibly some Dark Eras content <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a>'s <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire\" target=\"_blank\">BITE ME: How to Write Vampire</a> has me inspired and I'm percolating on how to play with the concept of the First Tradition, different attitudes towards and methods of feeding, how vampires relate to others, and different ways to Climb the Ladder or Spin the Web. Also, stuff for the Half-Damned, and possibly something about designing Clans.</li> <li><b>Werewolf:</b> Something akin to a Night Horrors book. Lots of Spirits, lots of territories; things about how I see the Hisil's ecology. Possibly stuff set in the Sundered World, or dealing with remnants of the Border Marches, that's seriously caught my imagination. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1757\" data-vbnamecard=\"1757\">Acrozatarim</a>'s particular brand of body horror, animism, and Spirit-empowered witchcraft is a current I can definitely swim in, so I'm also pondering writing a ton of Rites and playing with Influences a bit. Possibly making something for Rank 6+ Spirits (and Ephemeral Beings in general) inspired by <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, the rules for Things That Should Not Be from <b>Second Sight</b>, and some of the unofficial Rank 6+ Pangaeans.</li> <li><b>Mage: </b>There is an absolutely absurd amount of Dark Eras stuff frothing in my brain here, especially when it comes to concepts like Great Cults, Darshanas, and how the Mutapa Mages were presented in <b>Princes of the Conquered Land</b>. More cross-splat weirdness inspired by the aforesaid Dark Era, overhauls of Artifacts, Imbued Items, and Supernal Summoning (possibly Supernal Beings in general). Reworking Mage Sight to slot into the Investigation rules, and the Duel Arcane more properly into either Social Maneuvering or Chases. A whole lot of stuff on how I see the Supernal World (and why it isn't really separate or distant from the Fallen World), how to portray Mages in ways that fit folklore and traditional practices more closely than pop culture, emphasizing the drift Mages experience from human to something Other, and how to work with Mages so they don't completely overwhelm other magic users in the setting.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Mage Dark Eras and Spirit ecologies get my votes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T11:39:11-08:00","id":1279005,"title":"","content":"I am seriously considering to get back on my Belgian Congo Beast/Geist Dark Era, polish what's already there and then write what's missing.<br /> <br /> I planned to do It once I had the Geist book in my hands, but it's lots of work and starting earlier would allow me to hopefully have it ready if Geist and Beast join the Vault. Would people be interested in that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-06T19:34:49-08:00","id":1279101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div clas